WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.465 --> 00:00:18.383
- [Evan] "When you believe a
thing, believe it all the way.

00:00:18.383 --> 00:00:22.050
Implicitly and
unquestionably," Walt Disney.

00:00:23.816 --> 00:00:25.423
I was unhappy.

00:00:25.423 --> 00:00:27.010
I started my business because I wanted

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.801
to help entrpreneurs.

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:31.295
I struggled so much to
get my first business

00:00:31.295 --> 00:00:33.805
off the ground and almost gave up.

00:00:33.805 --> 00:00:35.687
One of the worst days of my life

00:00:35.687 --> 00:00:38.809
was when I told my
business partner, "I quit."

00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:40.757
I was tired of putting in all this time,

00:00:40.757 --> 00:00:43.762
and effort, and money,
and not seeing results.

00:00:43.762 --> 00:00:46.502
I was tired of working for
less than minimum wage.

00:00:46.502 --> 00:00:49.295
I was tired of losing respect for myself

00:00:49.295 --> 00:00:52.045
and feeling like a total failure.

00:00:53.047 --> 00:00:55.246
I managed to pull through, beat the odds,

00:00:55.246 --> 00:00:57.172
and be one of the success stories.

00:00:57.172 --> 00:00:59.075
And I wanted to share my experience

00:00:59.075 --> 00:01:00.250
and advice with others.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.525
Because I almost didn't make it.

00:01:02.525 --> 00:01:04.945
I wanted to make their
path a little easier

00:01:04.945 --> 00:01:06.983
then what I had to go through.

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:08.862
But I was unhappy.

00:01:08.862 --> 00:01:10.492
I was unhappy because I started doing

00:01:10.492 --> 00:01:12.053
all sorts of different projects.

00:01:12.053 --> 00:01:14.330
A website, YouTube videos, radio shows,

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:16.342
media interviews, and so on.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.640
But I wasn't getting people talking

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.840
about my business enough.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.427
It seemed too scattered.

00:01:21.427 --> 00:01:22.592
People couldn't wrap their heads around

00:01:22.592 --> 00:01:25.594
what I did, because it
was all over the place.

00:01:25.594 --> 00:01:27.455
I needed clarity.

00:01:27.455 --> 00:01:29.300
I thought it was a marketing problem.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.488
So I met with a friend, Jason,

00:01:30.488 --> 00:01:32.447
to try to come up with a
tagline for my business.

00:01:32.447 --> 00:01:34.745
Over the years it had gone from,

00:01:34.745 --> 00:01:36.870
"Helping You Build the
Company of Your Dreams,"

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.511
to, Motivation and Strategies
for Entrepreneurs,"

00:01:39.511 --> 00:01:42.952
to, "Over 20 Million Entrepreneurs
Helped and Counting."

00:01:42.952 --> 00:01:43.869
Weak sauce.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.668
What we came up with was,
"Hungry Entrepreneurs

00:01:47.668 --> 00:01:48.678
"Deserve Help."

00:01:48.678 --> 00:01:51.816
This felt better, but
still wasn't quite right.

00:01:51.816 --> 00:01:53.343
Something was missing and I couldn't

00:01:53.343 --> 00:01:55.391
put my finger on it.

00:01:55.391 --> 00:01:58.306
Then Steve Jobs changed my life.

00:01:58.306 --> 00:02:00.177
One day I stumbled upon what would become

00:02:00.177 --> 00:02:03.927
one of my favorite YouTube
videos of all time.

00:02:03.927 --> 00:02:06.655
It was Steve Jobs,
talking about marketing.

00:02:06.655 --> 00:02:08.724
It hit on exactly what I was missing.

00:02:08.724 --> 00:02:11.990
The core selling that
made Apple so successful.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:15.531
It had a dramatic impact
on my business and my life.

00:02:15.531 --> 00:02:18.114
Here's part of what Steve said.

00:06:18.781 --> 00:06:20.392
- If you act on what Steve Jobs said,

00:06:20.392 --> 00:06:22.496
you'll spark a movement.

00:06:22.496 --> 00:06:24.203
This speech was given
just after Steve Jobs

00:06:24.203 --> 00:06:25.907
returned to Apple.

00:06:25.907 --> 00:06:28.294
In his absence, Apple had struggled.

00:06:28.294 --> 00:06:30.757
It was a few months away from bankruptcy,

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:32.669
had only 4% market share,

00:06:32.669 --> 00:06:36.856
and was losing over a
billion dollars a year.

00:06:36.856 --> 00:06:40.253
Asking Jobs to come back
was a desperation move.

00:06:40.253 --> 00:06:43.118
Apple had just been through
three different CEOs

00:06:43.118 --> 00:06:45.430
and nobody could make it work.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.305
Jobs agreed, and took his company

00:06:47.305 --> 00:06:49.402
from life support to being the most

00:06:49.402 --> 00:06:52.366
valuable company in the world.

00:06:52.366 --> 00:06:54.304
It might be the single,
greatest turn around story

00:06:54.304 --> 00:06:55.304
of all time.

00:06:56.154 --> 00:06:58.892
It's time for your business
to start taking off too.

00:06:58.892 --> 00:07:01.020
In this speech, Jobs outlines the basics

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.004
of core selling.

00:07:03.004 --> 00:07:06.367
The way to do that is not to
talk about speeds and feeds.

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:08.718
It's not to talk about bits and megahertz.

00:07:08.718 --> 00:07:10.592
That's feature selling.

00:07:10.592 --> 00:07:12.931
"It's not to talk about why
we're better than Windows.

00:07:12.931 --> 00:07:15.307
"And what we're about isn't making boxes

00:07:15.307 --> 00:07:17.194
"for people to get their jobs done,

00:07:17.194 --> 00:07:19.391
"although we do that well."

00:07:19.391 --> 00:07:20.931
That's benefit selling.

00:07:20.931 --> 00:07:23.169
Marketing is about values.

00:07:23.169 --> 00:07:24.878
"We have to be really
clear on what we want

00:07:24.878 --> 00:07:26.993
"them to know about us.

00:07:26.993 --> 00:07:28.840
"Apple, at the core, it's core value

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:31.242
"is that we believe
that people with passion

00:07:31.242 --> 00:07:33.567
"can change the world for the better.

00:07:33.567 --> 00:07:35.127
"That's what we believe.

00:07:35.127 --> 00:07:37.029
"And we believe that, in this world,

00:07:37.029 --> 00:07:39.489
"people can change it for the better.

00:07:39.489 --> 00:07:41.168
"And that those people who are crazy

00:07:41.168 --> 00:07:43.428
"enough to think they
can change the world,

00:07:43.428 --> 00:07:45.940
"are the ones that actually do."

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.203
That's core selling.

00:07:48.203 --> 00:07:49.120
Mind blown.

00:07:50.638 --> 00:07:52.535
I finally had some clarity.

00:07:52.535 --> 00:07:55.326
It was time to get to work.

00:07:55.326 --> 00:07:57.489
If you want to model Steve
Jobs' amazing results,

00:07:57.489 --> 00:07:59.134
you need to get just as clear

00:07:59.134 --> 00:08:01.588
about who you are and what you stand for.

00:08:01.588 --> 00:08:05.300
Once you have clarity,
everything else falls into place.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.788
I was frustrated that my business didn't

00:08:06.788 --> 00:08:08.098
have enough momentum.

00:08:08.098 --> 00:08:09.824
And I didn't have the clarity I needed

00:08:09.824 --> 00:08:11.149
to move forward.

00:08:11.149 --> 00:08:14.786
So I made a list, to try
to find my core value.

00:08:14.786 --> 00:08:16.311
I started with my, "Hungry Entrepreneurs

00:08:16.311 --> 00:08:17.712
"Deserve Help," tagline.

00:08:17.712 --> 00:08:19.145
I wrote down ideas of how to convey

00:08:19.145 --> 00:08:21.126
the emotion behind my work.

00:08:21.126 --> 00:08:23.849
Something that really
got my blood pumping.

00:08:23.849 --> 00:08:25.588
I purposely tried not to think too much.

00:08:25.588 --> 00:08:27.312
Instead just started writing whatever

00:08:27.312 --> 00:08:28.912
entered my mind.

00:08:28.912 --> 00:08:30.748
Here's what I came up with.

00:08:30.748 --> 00:08:32.750
"Hungry Entrepreneurs Deserve Help."

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:36.036
What I do, what I believe,
but not inspirational.

00:08:36.036 --> 00:08:38.363
"Entrepreneurs change the world."

00:08:38.363 --> 00:08:40.038
"Entrepreneurs are heroes."

00:08:40.038 --> 00:08:41.501
"Celebrate Entrepreneurs."

00:08:41.501 --> 00:08:42.924
"Rallying Cry."

00:08:42.924 --> 00:08:44.587
"Gets your heart pumping."

00:08:44.587 --> 00:08:45.862
"It's on you."

00:08:45.862 --> 00:08:46.940
"Take your shot."

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:47.814
"Believe."

00:08:47.814 --> 00:08:48.877
"Follow your passion."

00:08:48.877 --> 00:08:50.013
"Overcome."

00:08:50.013 --> 00:08:51.275
"Persevere."

00:08:51.275 --> 00:08:52.190
"Keep going."

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.137
"Step Up."

00:08:53.137 --> 00:08:54.189
"Don't Settle."

00:08:54.189 --> 00:08:55.713
"Start."

00:08:55.713 --> 00:08:57.915
I didn't love anything on the list yet.

00:08:57.915 --> 00:09:00.063
Nothing felt quite right, yet.

00:09:00.063 --> 00:09:02.396
So I decided to sleep on it.

00:09:03.713 --> 00:09:05.709
If you're struggling to make a decision,

00:09:05.709 --> 00:09:08.175
sleep on it and see how
you feel in the morning.

00:09:08.175 --> 00:09:09.739
I felt inspired by Steve Jobs,

00:09:09.739 --> 00:09:11.589
and was ready to act but was frustrated

00:09:11.589 --> 00:09:13.563
that I couldn't get my clarity.

00:09:13.563 --> 00:09:16.037
I wanted it badly but it wasn't coming.

00:09:16.037 --> 00:09:18.287
So I slept on it.

00:09:18.287 --> 00:09:19.988
I came back to the same
list, the next day,

00:09:19.988 --> 00:09:21.839
and one word jumped out.

00:09:21.839 --> 00:09:23.424
"Believe."

00:09:23.424 --> 00:09:25.800
it was right there, in
the middle of my list.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.151
I thought about what believe meant to me.

00:09:28.151 --> 00:09:29.578
I came up with this.

00:09:29.578 --> 00:09:31.939
Believe in what you're doing, passion.

00:09:31.939 --> 00:09:34.076
Believe that you can do it, confidence.

00:09:34.076 --> 00:09:36.213
Believe that it will work, conviction.

00:09:36.213 --> 00:09:38.840
Finally, because I felt, "believe,"

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.476
on its' own was too simple,

00:09:40.476 --> 00:09:42.563
I started looking for ways to add to it.

00:09:42.563 --> 00:09:43.912
Believe you can.

00:09:43.912 --> 00:09:44.939
Believe in the possible.

00:09:44.939 --> 00:09:45.839
Believe more.

00:09:45.839 --> 00:09:46.764
Believe it all.

00:09:46.764 --> 00:09:47.638
Believe in belief.

00:09:47.638 --> 00:09:48.875
Believe in believe.

00:09:48.875 --> 00:09:51.252
The more I look at the list,

00:09:51.252 --> 00:09:54.201
the more I realize that
I just like, believe.

00:09:54.201 --> 00:09:56.912
So I decided I was going
to do this crazy thing

00:09:56.912 --> 00:10:00.462
and rebrand my entire
business around, "believe."

00:10:00.462 --> 00:10:04.963
It felt right, and my
life was about to change.

00:10:04.963 --> 00:10:06.449
The one thing that hit me pretty quickly

00:10:06.449 --> 00:10:08.560
was that this was more than just a slogan.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:09.926
This was a value.

00:10:09.926 --> 00:10:11.762
This was a personal mission statement.

00:10:11.762 --> 00:10:13.679
This was a way of life.

00:10:14.675 --> 00:10:17.013
"Believe," became #believe.

00:10:17.013 --> 00:10:18.840
It started my movement.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:20.349
I look back at the people that I

00:10:20.349 --> 00:10:21.877
had hired on my team,

00:10:21.877 --> 00:10:22.875
and the ones who were still with me

00:10:22.875 --> 00:10:25.675
were the ones who also had
believe as a core value.

00:10:25.675 --> 00:10:27.350
I reflected on my personal life

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.711
and realized that I'd always been

00:10:28.711 --> 00:10:31.513
about believing but I never realized it.

00:10:31.513 --> 00:10:32.964
I loved reading books about the little guy

00:10:32.964 --> 00:10:35.575
who overcame the odds, to be successful.

00:10:35.575 --> 00:10:36.862
My favorite book is, Seabiscuit.

00:10:36.862 --> 00:10:39.263
Which is the story of
an undersized racehorse

00:10:39.263 --> 00:10:40.425
who's victories lifted a nation

00:10:40.425 --> 00:10:43.600
in the middle of The Great Depression.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.701
My favorite entrepreneur is A.P. Giannini,

00:10:45.701 --> 00:10:48.226
the founder of Bank of America.

00:10:48.226 --> 00:10:50.239
Who made loans of as little as $25

00:10:50.239 --> 00:10:52.148
to people who's only collateral

00:10:52.148 --> 00:10:54.452
was the callouses on their hands.

00:10:54.452 --> 00:10:56.890
He would lend money based on a man's face

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:58.223
and a signature.

00:10:59.072 --> 00:11:00.652
My friends are about, "Believe."

00:11:00.652 --> 00:11:02.314
The songs I like are about, "Believe."

00:11:02.314 --> 00:11:04.088
Everything that makes me come alive,

00:11:04.088 --> 00:11:05.989
somehow relates to, "Believe."

00:11:05.989 --> 00:11:09.613
"Believe," isn't a
marketing slogan for me.

00:11:09.613 --> 00:11:11.613
It's who I am.

00:11:11.613 --> 00:11:13.728
You need to find who you are.

00:11:13.728 --> 00:11:17.895
Then you can start making
some important decisions.

